    // ---------- Added guide texts (plain language, minimal jargon) ----------
    "nisaSectionGuide": "This is your tax-free savings account. Money that grows inside it is not taxed. To begin with, all you really need to decide is how much you can put in each month. You can leave anything you are unsure about blank and still get a projection.",
    "expectedReturnGuide": "This is how much you assume your money grows each year, as a percentage. For a broadly diversified share portfolio held for many years, 3\u20135% is a cautious assumption. Nobody knows what markets will actually do, so treat it as a what-if number. A higher figure makes the result look better, but it is also more likely to be wrong.",
    "netWorthChartGuide": "This chart shows how your money is projected to change year by year, based on what you entered. The peak is the highest point your savings reach; the right-hand edge is the balance at the age you set as your life expectancy. The chart updates as soon as you change a number, so try things like saving more each month, or working a few years longer, and compare.",

