    "annualCashflowGuide": "This table shows how money moves each year. It starts with the assets available at the start of that year, reflects pension income and investment growth, then subtracts living costs, healthcare, taxes, insurance and loan payments to show what is left at year-end. All figures are projections. Private pension payments can include transfers from the policy reserve, so simply adding and subtracting every column may not exactly match investment-related gains or losses and other asset movements.",
